# Line endings.
#
# This repo is authored on Windows and RUN on Linux (PACE). A shell script or
# Slurm batch file that reaches the cluster with CRLF fails in a way that reads
# as nonsense -- `$'\r': command not found`, or `bad interpreter: /bin/bash^M`
# -- and the job dies before doing anything.
#
# Nothing is currently broken: every script is stored LF in the repository, and
# core.autocrlf=true is already normalising on commit. This file makes that
# guarantee explicit rather than dependent on each clone's config, and pins the
# WORKING copy of shell scripts to LF (eol=lf) so an editor cannot put CRs back.
#
# Note when checking this yourself: piping `git cat-file` through Git Bash can
# introduce CRLF into the pipe, so `git cat-file blob X | grep -c $'\r'` reports
# CRLF for files that are pure LF in the object store. Read the bytes with
# something that does not decode -- e.g. Python's read_bytes()/subprocess with
# capture_output -- before concluding anything.

* text=auto

*.sh      text eol=lf
*.sbatch  text eol=lf
*.bash    text eol=lf

# Binary assets git should never line-ending-convert or try to diff.
*.png     binary
*.jpg     binary
*.jpeg    binary
*.mp4     binary
*.npz     binary
*.ply     binary
*.parquet binary
*.pkl     binary
